WEBVTT

00:00:00.010 --> 00:00:03.430
An unexpected message says you must act
immediately to keep

00:00:03.430 --> 00:00:07.550
a service. Urgency can push you to skip
checks. Pause

00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:11.890
before opening the link or providing
information. Find the organization

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:16.910
through a known website or contact method,
then verify the claim independently.

00:00:19.229 --> 00:00:22.949
A video meeting may need camera access. A
simple text

00:00:22.949 --> 00:00:27.409
page usually does not. Grant permissions
only when they fit

00:00:27.409 --> 00:00:30.509
a clear task and you trust the app. You
can

00:00:30.509 --> 00:00:36.929
deny an unrelated request and review
camera or microphone permissions after you
finish.

00:00:38.888 --> 00:00:42.108
Do not plug in an unknown USB drive to
discover

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:46.088
who owns it. Give it to authorized staff.
Encryption makes

00:00:46.088 --> 00:00:50.988
data unreadable without a key. Read-only
settings restrict editing,

00:00:51.468 --> 00:00:55.408
which is a different protection. A locked
or encrypted device

00:00:55.408 --> 00:00:58.188
still needs careful account and file
access.

00:01:00.266 --> 00:01:04.026
Online safety also includes attention and
wellbeing. Catfishing

00:01:04.026 --> 00:01:07.706
uses a false identity to build trust. Fear
of missing

00:01:07.706 --> 00:01:11.106
out can make it hard to stop checking
alerts. Set

00:01:11.106 --> 00:01:16.026
useful notification limits, take breaks,
and seek support when online

00:01:16.026 --> 00:01:18.786
behavior makes you feel pressured or
unsafe.

00:01:20.793 --> 00:01:25.213
Choose one practice scenario and explain
your next step to

00:01:25.213 --> 00:01:29.433
a partner. Name the evidence, the
independent source you would

00:01:29.433 --> 00:01:33.233
check, and the action that limits risk.
Then complete the

00:01:33.233 --> 00:01:37.793
skills challenge and post-test. Use the
results to choose a

00:01:37.793 --> 00:01:39.313
task for more practice.
